      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "The Global Initiative for Asthma (GINA) provides effective medical care to asthmatic patients. Knowledge and appropriate handling of GINAS' management guidelines for medicine residents significantly reduce asthma morbidity and mortality."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To evaluate the level of knowledge about asthma on Global initiative for Asthma program before and after an educational strategy in residents."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIAL AND METHODS",
          "content": "Forty-four residents of first, second, and third grade of UMF No. 21 and No. 28 took part in this project A magisterial lecture and a workshop about clinical cases on asthma were carried out. The lecture lasted three hours and asthma surveys, before and after the educational strategy; were applied. Descriptive statistics as well as t test in SPSS were used for statistical analysis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Average grade of the 44 residents before the workshop was of 4.24 +/- 1.6, and after the workshop of 6.00 +/- 1.71. Therewere no significant differences among groups peryear of medical residency onthe initial assessment; however, residents of first year showed an increment on asthma knowledge (p < 0.05) in the subsequent test. There were no differences among groups."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Asthma educational workshops increase residents' awareness of asthma, mainly first-year medical students."
        }
      ]},
